From e3f20935482ea3578dc3e8319c6db9ac88a95aae Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Project SunUEFI <slwyts@tuta.io>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 09:13:34 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] leds: flash: leds-qcom-flash: Fix safety timer encoding

The MVFLASH safety timer encodes the first 10 ms period as zero in
bits 6:0. Bit 7 separately enables the timer. The downstream PM8350C
driver and the PMI8998 and PM8150L implementations use this encoding.

The current calculation adds a period to an enabled timeout, except
at the 1280 ms limit where clamping already produces the maximum code.
Subtract one from the number of 10 ms periods when it is nonzero.
Keep the enable decision based on the requested timeout: 10 ms sets
bit 7 even though the duration field is zero, while torch mode still
disables the timer.

Fixes: 96a2e242a5dc ("leds: flash: Add driver to support flash LED module in QCOM PMICs")
Link: https://github.com/MiCode/Xiaomi_Kernel_OpenSource/blob/45fb9bd6ae5ba2942fc1d53e4b6b46ef76992f71/drivers/leds/leds-qti-flash.c#L245
Link: https://github.com/OnePlusOSS/android_kernel_oneplus_msm8998/blob/e34b770a6350cab6bfd51d7b4c106b95b40b3dc5/drivers/leds/leds-qpnp-flash-v2.c#L101
Link: https://github.com/OnePlusOSS/android_kernel_oneplus_sm8150/blob/74eb3cd94e7cd70bb8a3983148b298851ea35123/drivers/leds/leds-qpnp-flash-v2.c#L1570
---
 drivers/leds/flash/leds-qcom-flash.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/leds/flash/leds-qcom-flash.c b/drivers/leds/flash/leds-qcom-flash.c
index a51d7662a7c35cb7d60802a5543a44b1ca324dcc..91fce899544ff6efaee4ce5d2437845b11a7322a 100644
--- a/drivers/leds/flash/leds-qcom-flash.c
+++ b/drivers/leds/flash/leds-qcom-flash.c
@@ -398,6 +398,9 @@ static int set_flash_timeout(struct qcom_flash_led *led, u32 timeout_ms)
 		chan_id = led->chan_id[i];
 
 		timer = timeout_ms / FLASH_TIMER_STEP_MS;
+		/* The first 10 ms period is encoded as zero. */
+		if (timer)
+			timer--;
 		timer = clamp_t(u8, timer, 0, FLASH_TIMER_VAL_MASK);
 
 		if (timeout_ms)
